        <div class="editorial reveal">
          <h2>Content is free. Commitment is not.</h2>
          <div class="thesis-text" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            <p>
              PageRank solved 1996 with hyperlinks — costly acts that were hard to fake at scale. In 2026, links are easy. AI generates content, reviews, and citations at zero marginal cost. The information layer has collapsed into self-referential noise.
            </p>
            <p>
              But there is a category of signal that remains structurally hard to fake: <strong>commitment</strong>. A repeat purchase. A decade of profitable operation. A customer who returns after a price increase. These acts require real cost — time, money, skin in the game. No AI can manufacture them at scale without bearing that cost.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
